Key insight on `jumpToTail`:

```dart
Future<List<SessionRecord>> jumpToTail() async {
  await _reAnchorToTail();
  while (_hasOlder &&
      _entries.length < _residentRecordCap &&
      _residentWindowBytes < _residentByteCap) {
    final joined = await loadOlder();
    if (joined.isEmpty) break;
  }
  return _windowBranch();
}
```

`loadOlder()` calls `_evictToBound(newestSide: true)` at the end — if entries exceed the cap, the NEWEST side (the tail we just anchored!) gets dropped. And `_dropNewest()` increments `_belowCount` (which was set to 0 by `_reAnchorToTail`) → `_belowCount = 1, 2, ...`. Then `hasNewer` becomes true again!

Loop condition check: `loadOlder` reads up to 8 chunks × defaultChunkRecords each before evicting. So after `_reAnchorToTail` (window = 1 chunk), if the resident cap is, say, 400 records and a chunk is 200 records: loop iteration 1: entries=200 < 400 → loadOlder reads one chunk → 400 entries, no eviction (cap not exceeded — eviction while `_entries.length > cap`, i.e. 400 > 400 false). Loop check: 400 < 400 false → stop. OK.

But if defaultChunkRecords × 8 in one loadOlder call overshoots the cap... e.g. cap = 400, chunk = 200: loadOlder reads chunk (400 entries), `joined.isNotEmpty` → break after first pass (maxChunks 8 but breaks when joined non-empty). So loadOlder reads ONE chunk when records join the branch. Each chunk ≤ 200 records (maxRecords default). So the max entries after a loadOlder = current + chunkRecords. Eviction only triggers if entries > cap after the read. Loop guard ensures entries < cap before, so after one chunk: entries < cap + chunkRecords — could exceed cap → newest-side eviction drops chunkRecords−(cap−entriesBefore)... wait no: eviction drops until length ≤ cap. Records dropped from the NEWEST side → tail evicted → `_belowCount` rises above 0 → `hasNewer` true → banner reappears right after a jump-to-tail! Hmm, but wait: `_dropNewest` only drops if length > cap strictly. entries before < cap, after adding one chunk of ≤ defaultChunkRecords... when does defaultChunkRecords exceed the remaining headroom? Let me find the constants.

Also: does `loadOlder` evict when `_belowCount` was 0? `_dropNewest`: `if (_belowCount != null) _belowCount = _belowCount! + 1` — yes, from 0 → 1. And `hasNewer` getter — let me check.

Let me find the cap constants and the hasNewer getter.

